# The whole point: your implementation is disposable, the tests are not.
practice/katas/*/src/

# drill state and your start date — local, not the repo's.
#
# practice/decks/.state.json is NOT here on purpose: a card's Leitner box is the
# evidence bar for the whole E group and for Y1, so it is proof, not preference.
# It is the only evidence artifact that used to be untracked, and losing it would
# lose every capability the deck scores.
logs/.drill_state.json
logs/.bughunt_state.json
# Snapshots of your own passing solutions, kept only so `make hunt` has something to
# mutate. Still your code, still disposable, still never committed.
logs/.snapshots/
logs/.start_date

# the calendar with your real dates stamped in. plan/CALENDAR.md is the committed
# one and carries relative day labels, because the start date is not a repo fact.
plan/CALENDAR.dated.md

# job-search material never belongs in a public training repo
plan/APPLICATIONS.md
plan/private/

# build output
build/
*.o
*.out
a.out

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Working notes from the audits. Never committed: they are snapshots of the repo at one
# moment with a fix list attached, and once the list is worked through they describe a repo
# that no longer exists. Anything in them worth keeping gets folded into the documents it
# belongs to — plan/COVERAGE.md for decisions, the tool docstrings for why a check exists.
TMP_AUDIT.md
AUDIT_TASKS.md
